    "summary": "Per-field @ts-expect-error checks (verdict, severity, dimension, artifactId) only catch those specific names -- adding any other field, e.g. scopeId, would leave every existing check passing. Added a type-level Equal<keyof T, ...> assertion for both CommentEntry and ReviewContextRound: it fails to compile for an added or removed key of any name, since keyof T would then differ from the expected literal union. Verified by temporarily adding an unrelated scopeId field and confirming the typecheck fixture now fails to compile, then restoring.",
